}\line\b0 The evaluation criteria for the Smart Fashion Advisor system are based on standard performance metrics used in classification and prediction systems. These metrics help in analyzing both the accuracy of skin tone detection and the reliability of the recommendation process. Accuracy represents the overall correctness of the system by measuring how many predictions are correctly classified out of the total inputs. A higher accuracy value indicates that the system performs well in identifying skin tones correctly.\par
Precision measures the proportion of correctly predicted positive instances among all predicted positives. A high precision value ensures that the system minimizes incorrect recommendations, which is important for maintaining user trust. Recall, also known as sensitivity, measures the system\rquote s ability to correctly identify all relevant instances. A higher recall value reduces the chances of missing correct classifications, which directly impacts recommendation quality.\par
The F1-Score provides a balance between precision and recall, making it useful when both false positives and false negatives need to be minimized. Additionally, error-based metrics such as Mean Absolute Error (MAE) and Root Mean Square Error (RMSE) are used to evaluate prediction accuracy. Lower values of these metrics indicate better performance and fewer errors in prediction. These evaluation criteria collectively ensure a comprehensive assessment of the system\rquote s effectiveness and reliability in real-world scenarios [4][8][11][12].\b\par
