\b0 The performance comparison table illustrates the improvements in fashion recommendation systems over time with the integration of advanced technologies such as machine learning, deep learning, and hybrid approaches. Earlier systems based on traditional machine learning techniques achieved moderate accuracy levels, as they primarily relied on user history and basic filtering methods. In 2018, hybrid recommendation systems improved performance by combining multiple techniques, leading to better F1-scores and overall recommendation quality.\par
With the introduction of deep learning models, particularly convolutional neural networks, systems achieved higher precision and recall values by effectively analyzing visual features of clothing items. Recent AI-based systems have further enhanced performance by incorporating personalization and real-time interaction, resulting in improved recall and user satisfaction.\par
The proposed Smart Fashion Advisor system demonstrates competitive performance by combining computer vision, rule-based color mapping, and dataset filtering. Although it does not rely entirely on deep learning for recommendations, it achieves efficient and accurate results due to its lightweight and optimized architecture. The system shows an estimated improvement over traditional methods in terms of accuracy and usability. This comparison highlights the effectiveness of hybrid approaches in delivering practical and scalable solutions in the fashion domain [2][6][7][9].\b\par
\par
VII. COMPUTER VISION SYSTEM FOR SKIN TONE ANALYSIS AND OUTFIT RECOMMENDATION\b0\par
Computer vision systems have significantly improved the process of analyzing human features and generating personalized recommendations in various domains, including fashion. The Smart Fashion Advisor system utilizes computer vision techniques to analyze facial features and determine the user\rquote s skin tone, which serves as a key parameter for generating outfit suggestions. By automating this process, the system eliminates the need for manual input and ensures consistent and objective recommendations. The use of MediaPipe Face Mesh enables accurate detection of facial landmarks, allowing the system to focus on specific regions such as the cheeks and forehead for reliable skin tone extraction [4][12].\par
The system begins by capturing or uploading an image, which is then processed using image preprocessing techniques such as resizing, normalization, and noise reduction. These steps ensure that the input image is suitable for further analysis. The facial landmark detection module identifies key regions, and pixel-level color information is extracted using OpenCV. This information is used to classify the skin tone into predefined categories. The classification process is efficient and does not require extensive model training, making it suitable for real-time applications [11][4].\par
Once the skin tone is identified, the system applies color theory principles to map the detected tone to a set of recommended colors. These colors are then used to filter a structured fashion dataset, generating personalized outfit suggestions. The system considers additional attributes such as gender, category, and usage to provide relevant and context-aware recommendations. This integration of computer vision and data filtering ensures that the system delivers accurate and meaningful results [5][8].\par
Furthermore, the system provides real-time visualization of results through a web-based interface developed using Flask. Users can view their detected skin tone, recommended color palettes, and suggested outfits instantly. The inclusion of a chatbot enhances interaction by providing additional styling advice. Overall, the Smart Fashion Advisor demonstrates how computer vision can be effectively applied to build intelligent and user-friendly fashion recommendation systems [9][10].\par
\par
\b VIII. FUTURE SCOPE\b0\par
The Smart Fashion Advisor system provides a strong foundation for personalized fashion recommendation; however, there are several opportunities for further enhancement and expansion. One of the key areas for improvement is the integration of deep learning-based recommendation models. By incorporating techniques such as convolutional neural networks (CNNs) and neural collaborative filtering, the system can learn from user behavior and preferences, enabling more accurate and dynamic recommendations over time. This would allow the system to move beyond rule-based logic and provide adaptive personalization [1][3].\par
Another important enhancement is the inclusion of real-time fashion trends and external data sources. Integrating APIs from fashion platforms or social media can help the system stay updated with current trends and provide more relevant suggestions. Additionally, expanding the dataset to include a wider variety of clothing styles, brands, and cultural preferences can improve the diversity and inclusivity of recommendations. The system can also be extended to support multiple languages, making it accessible to a broader audience.\par
The implementation of advanced technologies such as Augmented Reality (AR) and Virtual Try-On systems can further improve user experience. These features would allow users to visualize how outfits look on them before making decisions. Moreover, developing a mobile application version of the system can enhance accessibility and convenience. Cloud-based deployment can also improve scalability and performance for large-scale usage.\par
Finally, improving the robustness of skin tone detection under varying lighting conditions and different camera qualities is an important area of future work. Incorporating adaptive preprocessing techniques and more advanced models can enhance accuracy and reliability. These enhancements would make the Smart Fashion Advisor a more intelligent, scalable, and user-centric solution for modern fashion recommendation systems [10][16].\b\par
\par
IX. CONCLUSION\par
\b0 The Smart Fashion Advisor system presents an effective and practical solution for personalized outfit recommendation by integrating computer vision, rule-based intelligence, and data-driven techniques. The system successfully analyzes facial images to detect the user\rquote s skin tone and utilizes this information to suggest suitable color palettes and clothing options. By automating the outfit selection process, it reduces the dependency on manual decision-making and provides consistent and reliable fashion recommendations. The use of efficient tools such as MediaPipe and OpenCV ensures accurate feature extraction, while Pandas-based dataset filtering enables scalable and real-time recommendation generation.\par
One of the key strengths of the system lies in its hybrid approach, which combines domain knowledge of color theory with computational techniques. This allows the system to deliver interpretable and meaningful recommendations without relying on complex deep learning models. The web-based implementation using Flask further enhances accessibility and usability, enabling users to interact with the system easily through image upload or live camera input. Additionally, the inclusion of a chatbot improves user engagement by providing real-time fashion advice and guidance.\par
Despite its effectiveness, the system has certain limitations, such as sensitivity to lighting conditions and reliance on predefined rules for recommendation. However, these limitations provide opportunities for future improvements, including the integration of adaptive learning models and real-time trend analysis. Overall, the Smart Fashion Advisor demonstrates the potential of AI-driven systems in transforming everyday lifestyle applications and highlights the importance of combining computer vision and data processing techniques for building intelligent and user-centric solutions.\par
